  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="475ef1ae-8079-51ca-96d0-42b7a51ce9b5" activityNameId="2f3bc677-6cdf-5933-a382-f133c17b17da" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Radioactive waste, in final repository for nuclear waste SF, HLW, and ILW</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Radioactive waste, in final repository for nuclear waste SF, HLW, and ILW
For operation is meant the input of the waste and the refilling of the tunnels. The waste volume includes always the steel or concrete container. The density of SF is approximately 7.6 tonne per m3, of HLW is about 7.1 tonne per m3, and of ILW is 2.5 tonne per m3. Considering the amounts of the three different waste class streams for the Swiss 192 GWa scenario, the average density for the radwaste to be disposed of in this geological repository is calculated as about 5.4 tonne per m3. The total electricity supplied from the grid has been estimated on the basis of the necessary power and the duration of the operation. For the transport of HLW and ILW, an average distance of 70 km between the intermediate repository and the preliminarly identified site has been considered. Seepage water and methane to air are assumed to be negligible.;
Synonyms: Conditioned Spent Fuel, High level radioactive waste, Intermediate level radioactive waste; 
UUID: 62835b0e-1eaf-40a3-b89b-0dec99d2cc14
This module includes: material and energy requirements; transports of vitrified and intermediate radioactive waste (non reprocessed spent fuel is included in the conditioning module) as well as materials; and, infrastructure requirement. This describes the operation of a repository for intermediate and long-lived low radioactive waste in the Swiss context. Seepage water and methane to air are not included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Currently available knowledge.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_62835b0e-1eaf-40a3-b89b-0dec99d2cc14.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
